      "message": "Hi @Sarthak, thanks for the effort!\nBTW, I wonder if this work is intended for Linux upstream? if yes, I wonder why we consider a per-inode verification digests rather than dm-verity-compatible metadata approach so that the same metadata can be used for dm-verity and erofs file-backed mounts.\nAlso the digest list is not absolutely secure since the on-disk metadata can still be compromised, and it complexs the EROFS metadata layout a lot (since we need to design digest metadata for each inode layout.)\nI once hope if there is not a particularly specific requirement, the verify metadata would be better to be dm-verity compatible, and it\u0027s totally decoupled from the erofs metadata details so it\u0027s simplifed.",
